class: runtime
profiles: standard
summary: the published network consumer runs a TCP server and its client and then two UDP sockets over 127.0.0.1 and over ::1 in one process, the client's lines sent through io.send and read back through a line reader, the server reading them through a line reader and echoing them through a buffered writer, each listener and socket on a free port it reads back, and reports what came back; a system without IPv6's loopback fails it and says so
program: main.ldn
root: ../../../../..
run_expect: output.txt
stream: output
status: 42
constructs: 0570, 0680, 0790, 0900, 0910, 0940, 1030, 1100, 1210, 1650, 1660
targets: linux-x86-64, linux-arm64, macos-arm64, freebsd-x86-64, freebsd-arm64, linux-rv64
